    "additionalProperties": false,
    "description": "Internal replacement tables: exact, regex, or mixed. Mixed uses string exact pairs plus regex_pairs, exact first; case_sensitive required for exact table, inline (?i) for regex. Each supplied rule replaces both tables. Boolean exact result_type uses true/false to.value and other null only. Exact result_type changes the constant type (omitted=input type); keys retain type, to/other.value use result_type. No automatic conversion of unmatched text. Different result_type requires other null/value, datetime requires null with local ISO whole seconds. Regex: string patterns, ordered first match replaces the whole cell with a literal string ($1 stays literal); omit case_sensitive/precision, use inline (?i), other keep/null only. Exact string rules require case_sensitive and omit precision. Integer/real rules require precision>=0 (hundredths) and omit case_sensitive; absolute inclusive tolerance, nearest key, ties choose larger. Nonzero precision adds real <field>_Delta=key-input. Large Int64 values must be decimal strings, never rounded JSON numbers. Existing-node patches preserve omitted rules and output_mode. Proposal external: exactly one additional table input 1, explicit roles, no duplicate-key priority. Preserve omitted rules and both existing port identities. Native roles must match key/result types. Other keep uses matching types; changed-type keep remains excluded."
